menu "SDIO soak test"

    config SOAK_URL
        string "Stream URL (http:// or https://)"
        default "https://icecast.radiofrance.fr/fip-midfi.mp3"
        help
            The stream to pull continuously. Run A (control): a FLAC/any large file on a
            LAN HTTP server (no internet, no TLS). Run B (real path): a public MP3 station
            over HTTPS. A finite file is re-opened when it ends (counted as `restart`).

    config SOAK_DURATION_MIN
        int "Test duration, minutes (0 = until reset)"
        default 120

    config SOAK_REPORT_SEC
        int "Report period, seconds"
        default 30

    config SOAK_RING_KB
        int "PSRAM ring buffer, KB"
        default 512
        help
            The consumer drains the ring at SOAK_DRAIN_KBPS; a stall shows up as the ring
            running empty. Big enough to hide short hiccups, small enough to expose stalls.

    config SOAK_DRAIN_KBPS
        int "Consumer drain rate, kbit/s (0 = drain as fast as data arrives)"
        default 128
        help
            Emulates the decoder pace. For the LAN file test set 0 (pure throughput) or a
            realistic FLAC rate (~1000).

    config SOAK_STALL_SEC
        int "Stall threshold: seconds without any received byte"
        default 5

    config SOAK_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "HTTP socket timeout, ms"
        default 10000

    config SOAK_PHASE_MIN
        int "Phase length, minutes (0 = no phases, one steady run)"
        default 0
        help
            With phases enabled the test walks SOAK_BALLAST_TARGETS, holding each for this
            long and printing a SOAK PHASE line at the start and a SOAK PHASE END summary at
            the finish. The bit-rate axis is driven from the other end (rate_server.py), so
            one run can cover a whole grid without a reflash.

    config SOAK_BALLAST_TARGETS
        string "Free DMA-SRAM targets per phase, KB, comma separated (0 = no ballast)"
        default "0"
        help
            Before each phase the test allocates DMA-capable internal SRAM until no more than
            this much is free, emulating the memory pressure the display, LVGL and the audio
            core put on the same pool. The player itself runs at about 27 KB free
            (docs/CONCEPT.md section 8), which is the point of the exercise: the link is not
            measured in isolation on the real device. List the targets from most free to
            least, because the tight ones are the ones that can end the run.

    config SOAK_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID override (empty = take from the player's NVS)"
        default ""

    config SOAK_WIFI_PASS
        string "Wi-Fi password override (empty = take from the player's NVS)"
        default ""

endmenu
